course: dictionary
lesson: 1810
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word clown can name a circus performer, but it can also be an insult. Two dads shout over a parking space outside school, «You weren't, you clown!» There is no circus there, so clown is an insult that means stupid or useless.
explain: Clown can also be a verb. To clown around means to behave in a silly way to make people laugh. The word around is a clue that you are meeting the verb, not the noun. Ask yourself: is this a person, or is this an action?
explain: Look for clues around the word. A circus, big shoes and face paint point to a performer. The class clown is someone who makes everyone laugh, often getting into trouble. A quarrel between two dads points to an insult. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A clown is a performer in a circus or at a party, who wears funny clothes, big shoes and face paint.
fact: The class clown is a child who often acts silly or makes jokes.
fact: Calling someone a clown can be an insult, meaning they are stupid or useless.
fact: To clown around means to behave in a silly way to make people laugh.
fact: Pierrot is a sad clown with a white face, so not every clown is happy.
exercise: Two dads shout over a parking space outside school, «You weren't, you clown!» What does clown mean here? | *An insult meaning stupid or useless | A fish with bright stripes | A performer in a circus | A party game
exercise: «She is the class clown.» What does class clown mean? | A teacher who tells jokes | A child who is always quiet | A child who cleans the classroom | *A child who makes everyone laugh, often getting into trouble
exercise: Which phrase shows that clown is a verb? | a circus clown | clown fish | class clown | *clown around
test: At the circus, the clown wore big shoes and face paint. What is a clown in this sentence? | *A performer who makes people laugh | A kind of fish | A pair of shoes | A teacher who marks homework
test: Pierrot is a sad clown with a white face. What does this tell you about clowns? | Clowns only live in the sea | Clowns cannot have faces | *Not every clown is always happy | Every clown is always happy
exam: «You weren't, you clown!» Which meaning of clown fits this sentence? | *Insult meaning stupid or useless | Circus performer | Party game | Type of fish
